# Third-party device frame assets

This project vendors transparent PNG device bezels and screen masks for
App Store marketing-style screenshot composition. Exports remain exact
App Store Connect pixel sizes.

## Sources

### 1. jonnyjackson26/device-frames-media
- Repo: https://github.com/jonnyjackson26/device-frames-media
- Used for: **iPhone 17 Pro Max (Deep Blue)**, iPad Pro 13" M4/M5,
  iPad Pro 11" M4/M5 (portrait + landscape Space Black)
- Previously: iPhone 16 Pro Max Black Titanium (superseded by 17 Pro Max;
  screen template geometry remains 1320×2868 within a 1520×3068 frame)
- Assets: `frame.png`, `mask.png`, `template.json` (screen rectangle)
- Vendored under: `public/frames/iphone/`, `public/frames/ipad-13/`,
  `public/frames/ipad-11/`
- Remote fallback / Vercel rewrites point at the Deep Blue 17 Pro Max paths
- License: No SPDX license file was published on the upstream repo at the
  time of vendoring. Assets are included as a community device-template
  dataset cited by this project; see the upstream README for contribution
  and usage context. If upstream licensing changes, prefer replacing these
  assets.

### 2. bunlongheng/frames (MIT)
- Repo: https://github.com/bunlongheng/frames
- License: MIT (Copyright (c) 2026 Bunlong Heng) — see upstream LICENSE
- Used for: MacBook Air Space Gray bezel (`macbook.png`) + screen geometry
  from `offsets.json`
- Vendored under: `public/frames/mac/`

### 3. bunlongheng/frames — iPhone Duo (foldable) (MIT)
- Same MIT repo as MacBook frames above
- Used for: **iPhone Duo closed** (`iphone-duo-closed-portrait.png`),
  **open portrait**, and **open landscape** bezels
- Screen holes measured by flood-fill of the transparent interior:
  closed 1398×2034 @ (88,80) in 1574×2194; open portrait 2007×2853 @
  (120,120) in 2247×3093; open landscape 2853×2007 @ (120,120) in 3093×2247
- Vendored under: `public/frames/iphone-duo/{closed,open-portrait,open-landscape}/`
- Why this source: Hoverify/Screeny Duo PNGs disallow redistribution as an
  asset pack; jal-co/iphone-duo ships Apple’s GLB (not openly licensed for
  bezel redistribution). bunlongheng/frames is MIT and already used here.

### 4. Apple Watch
- No suitable open transparent PNG Watch bezel was available in the
  preferred sources above (device-frames-media, bunlongheng/frames).
- Watch exports use a lightweight procedural bezel fallback drawn in
  canvas (`src/lib/frames.ts`) so the platform remains covered without
  redistributing Apple product imagery.

### 5. Fonts
- Google fonts (Outfit, Fraunces, Source Sans 3, JetBrains Mono) are
  self-hosted via `next/font/google` at build time (no runtime Google
  requests). Web-safe fonts (Arial, Georgia, Verdana, Trebuchet MS,
  Courier New, Times New Roman) use the system stack.
